<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>For purposes of this chapter, the following terms have the following meanings:</p><p>(a)<span class="EnSpace"/>“County placing agency” means the county social services department or county probation department.</p><p>(b)<span class="EnSpace"/>“Educational authority” means an entity designated to represent the interests of a child for educational and related services.</p><p>(c)<span class="EnSpace"/>“Homeless children and youths” and “unaccompanied youths” are as defined in Section 11434a(2) of Title 42 of the United States Code.</p><p>(d)<span class="EnSpace"/>“Local educational agency” means a school district, a county office
						of education, a charter school, or a special education local plan area.</p></caml:Content>